Quick Screen Off (fast, requires Shizuku)
Use Activity-based command for the most reliable triggering. After execution, the service automatically cleans up and exits.

Turn screen off:
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1

Turn screen on:
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 0

Turn screen off with auto-wake timer (N seconds later, screen turns back on automatically):
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1 --ei timer <seconds>
Example - turn screen off and auto-wake after 300 seconds (5 minutes):
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1 --ei timer 300
Example - turn screen off and auto-wake after 30 seconds:
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1 --ei timer 30

How timer works: the service stays alive as a foreground process, waits N seconds, then executes the reverse action (lights on / off) and exits. No background residue after completion.

Parameter volkey
    Set to 1 to enable volume key toggle during timer countdown.
    When enabled, pressing either volume key (up or down) will toggle the screen on/off WITHOUT cancelling the timer.
    The timer keeps running, and volume keys can be used repeatedly until the timer expires.
    The notification will show a "Cancel" button to manually cancel the timer at any time.
    Omit this parameter (default 0) to disable volume key monitoring.
    Only takes effect when used together with the timer parameter.
Example - turn screen off with 300s timer and volume key toggle:
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1 --ei timer 300 --ei volkey 1
Example - turn screen off with 30s timer, no volume key monitoring:
`am start -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.QuickScreenOffActivity --ei screen 1 --ei timer 30
How volkey works: uses getevent to monitor volume key presses via Shizuku. Idle monitoring has negligible battery impact (blocking read on input device). The notification's "Cancel" button stops the timer immediately. Lock screen unlock still cancels the timer automatically.

Quick Screen Off (root only, no Shizuku needed)
Use root privilege to directly execute the screen power control via app_process. No Shizuku required.

First, get your APK path:
`pm path own.moderpach.extinguish

Then use the returned path to execute:

Turn screen off:
`su -c 'CLASSPATH=<your_apk_path> app_process / own.moderpach.extinguish.service.RootScreenOff off'

Turn screen on:
`su -c 'CLASSPATH=<your_apk_path> app_process / own.moderpach.extinguish.service.RootScreenOff on'

Example (replace the path with your actual APK path from pm path):
`su -c 'CLASSPATH=/data/app/~~xxxx/own.moderpach.extinguish-yyyy/base.apk app_process / own.moderpach.extinguish.service.RootScreenOff off'


Extinguish Service (classic mode)
You can control the Extinguish service externally through the Android Debug Bridge (ADB).
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei <Parameter> <Value>
You can specify multiple parameters or no parameters. You need to add '--ei' before each specified parameter.

Parameter screen
    0 Turn screen on
    1 Turn screen off
    2 Switch screen state
Example
Turn screen on:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei screen 0
Turn screen off:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei screen 1
Switch screen state:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei screen 2

Parameter fb
    0 Show floating button
    1 Hide floating button
    2 Switch floating button state
* This parameter does not override the floating button enable setting
Example
Show floating button:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei fb 0
Hide floating button:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei fb 1
Switch floating button state:
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei fb 2

Parameter rfb
    1 Remove floating button in this service
* This parameter overrides the floating button enabled setting and is only valid when the Extinguish service is not running.
Example
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei rfb 1

Parameter stop
    1 Stop service
Example
`adb shell am startservice -n own.moderpach.extinguish/.service.ExtinguishService --ei stop 1
